posts.body:
I LOVE how the community came together to figure this out. You guys are awesome and thank you so much!!
@kelarly
Eyyyyyyy, thank you so much for considering the Epic Wings series!!
To answer your question both
@ShadowDragon
and
@ATT_Turan
are correct. It is an older game so it was created in MV and the plugin is AltMenuScreen although stripped of many of its rtp components like the RM window which can be found in the the pic/systems folder and using a custom images for all the windows in the menu created in gimp. As far as the menu facesets for the main screen I took the battler sprites from each character and used the animation that I liked the most from each and put it into a single enlarged faceset image so it’s not actually pulling any data from the characters to get the sprite. Just enlarged images created by me in gimp
. I hope this helps answer some questions and happy deving!
